# The now-playing cluster in the statusline. Headless runs paint the
# idle pair (the preferred player's mark and a play box) as the Rust dumps
# show it; `# env: MNML_NOW_PLAYING` puts a track on the row instead —
# the transport: pause, skip, `artist - title` — and a click on the play
# chip drives that player (mixr's transport is cut in this build: the
# toast says so). Row 38 is the statusline at 120x40; the cluster sits
# left of WRAP in the right lane.
# env: MNML_NOW_PLAYING=Karma Police|playing|mixr|Radiohead
write notes.txt hello
open notes.txt
expect screen contains "Karma Police"
expect screen lacks "󱼀"
click 23 38
expect screen contains "cut from mnml-zig"
